1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:31,698
<i>Lily's been through so much.</i>
<i>This won't take her down.</i>

6
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:35,410
<i>You're going to die. Poor, Ivy.</i>

7
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>I am Ivy Aguas. I can handle everything.</i>

8
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:42,250
[laughing]

9
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,210
<i>-Hello, Dad?</i>
<i>-Where are you? I'll help you.</i>

10
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:46,921
<i>We're going to save Ivy</i>
<i>no matter what happens.</i>

11
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:50,175
[Damian] <i>I'm here to help Ivy Aguas.</i>

12
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:51,968
[gunshots]

13
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,598
[Camia] <i>She still has to bring</i>
<i>those criminals to justice.</i>

14
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:59,309
[Julio] <i>You have been sleeping</i>
<i>with the enemy.</i>

15
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:01,728
<i>Your enemy, Governor. Not mine.</i>

16
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:03,021
[Diego] <i>We won't give up.</i>

17
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:07,525
<i>We'll keep fighting and remove</i>
<i>Julio Ardiente from power.</i>

18
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:12,113
<i>We can't let my daughter's</i>
<i>sacrifices be for nothing.</i>

19
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>Well, good luck to your endeavors,</i>
<i>Diego Torillo.</i>

20
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:17,285
<i>All your efforts will be in vain.</i>

21
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:19,079
[crowd chanting] <i>Cheater!</i>

22
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:19,996
<i>Come on, Emilia.</i>

23
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,873
[chuckling nervously]

24
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:24,083
<i>This is not happening. Come on.</i>

25
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:29,839
[Ivy] <i>Mark my words, Emilia.</i>
<i>If I die, I will haunt you.</i>

26
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,052
[screaming]

27
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:36,179
<i>Raul! Papa!</i>

28
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:40,350
-Papa!
-Hey! Hey! What?!

29
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:41,434
-Papa!
-What?

30
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:42,769
Papa. Papa.

31
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:44,395
We need to have this house blessed

32
00:01:44,479 --> 00:01:46,439
or start practicing feng shui, Papa.

33
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,566
What's wrong with this house?

34
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,026
Hold on. Didn't you have this place

35
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,152
blessed before moving in?

36
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,320
-No. But…
-Why?

37
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,404
[Julio] Look, look.

38
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:57,283
There is only one bad spirit
that's in this house right now,

39
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:00,912
and that is the cheap beer
that Raul is drinking.

40
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:03,081
Papa, I'm not joking! I saw a ghost!

41
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:06,835
I saw Ivy Aguas there!
I saw her there! I'm not joking!

42
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:09,546
Raul, please believe me!
Papa, I saw her there.

43
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:12,674
She was so close to me.
I could even smell her.

44
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:14,884
All right, enough, enough.
I bet it's all in your head.

45
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:18,388
-No! It's not!
-I say, Emilia, grow up.

46
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:20,390
There are no such things as ghosts.

47
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,100
No, Papa! You have to trust me this time!

48
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,812
I saw her! I saw Ivy Aguas there, Papa!

49
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:28,273
This is real. There really is a ghost.

50
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:31,776
She's haunting me.
Papa, she's haunting me.

51
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:35,363
You know what? This only means one thing.

52
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:40,952
That Ivy Aguas is truly dead.

53
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:45,456
And, if she's ever going to haunt someone,

54
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,250
[chuckling] it's definitely you.

55
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:51,337
No, Papa. No! No! No!

56
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,340
-Who's in there?!
-[screaming]

57
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:56,759
-[laughing]
-[screaming]

58
00:02:56,843 --> 00:03:00,054
Papa. [wailing]

59
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:02,807
[howling]

60
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:04,934
-[Julio] Whoo!
-I hate you both!

61
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,311
[Julio chuckles]

62
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:11,941
Ma'am?

63
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,445
Ma'am!

64
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:17,572
Ma'am?

65
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,161
I hate you! I hate you!

66
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:24,370
-What the--
-I hate you!

67
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:26,247
Stop it. Hold on.

68
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,082
[grunting]

69
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:30,043
-What is your problem?
-You.

70
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,295
You're my problem.

71
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:34,339
You tossed me aside.

72
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,841
You used me.

73
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:40,803
You took my men and my weapons

74
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:44,557
just so you could help
your worthless friends.

75
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:46,726
You're all the same.

76
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,519
And here I thought you were different.

77
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,105
You're another user!

78
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,315
You're so emotional.

79
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:54,025
You're overthinking things.

80
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:56,069
Just let me explain.

81
00:03:56,152 --> 00:03:59,739
Yes, you're right.
I went out to help my friends.

82
00:03:59,822 --> 00:04:01,991
I went out to look for Ivy Aguas.

83
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:05,245
But if you really want
to take the Ardientes down…

84
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:08,581
then, believe me,
we're going to need their help.

85
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,792
They're on our side.

86
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:16,130
So, where's your
amazing friend, Ivy Aguas?

87
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,384
I thought she wanted to be a superhero?

88
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,970
Well? What now?

89
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:23,846
She's dead.

90
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:26,808
She's dead!

91
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:35,775
[exhales]

92
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,945
I'm warning you, Madrigal.

93
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,323
Forget about those friends of yours.

94
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:47,412
Because I'm the only one who can help you.

95
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,958
[tense music playing]

96
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,344
[exhales]

97
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:10,518
Come on, Emilia. Don't be scared.

98
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:13,187
She's already dead.

99
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:15,648
She can't even hurt you.

100
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:18,359
She's dead. Just get a grip, Emilia!

101
00:05:20,737 --> 00:05:22,238
Come on, come on, come on.

102
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:25,366
Inhale, exhale. You can do it.

103
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:27,076
It's time to sleep.

104
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,037
[exhales]

105
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,290
[exhales]

106
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,669
-[glass breaks]
-[gasps]

107
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:44,510
[eerie music playing]

108
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:52,602
[loud thud]

109
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:05,823
Did you hear that?

110
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:22,131
That's it, Governor. Fifty million pesos.

111
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:23,758
Good.

112
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:26,260
So, who do you plan to give it to?

113
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:30,098
That is for our dear Martel.

114
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:33,893
So he can forget about our little deal

115
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,144
during the election.

116
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,771
Count it as insurance.

117
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:40,566
Can't be too careful.
He might just rat us out.

118
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,903
Especially now that these two birds,

119
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:50,201
by the name of Torillo and Ruiz,
are teaming up against me.

120
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,870
So it's true, Governor?

121
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:56,624
That they really can oust you
from your position?

122
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:58,960
Oust? Julio Ardiente?

123
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,503
[laughing]

124
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,505
Impossible.

125
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,674
The votes have been counted.

126
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:07,552
And I've been declared the winner.

127
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:11,180
Remember, I know politics
like the back of my hand.

128
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:17,979
Now, the only thing I hate,
Colonel, is all that fussing

129
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:21,315
while we plan
for the centennial celebration.

130
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:26,446
I'm sure you know the whole
province is watching us.

131
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:29,574
So, let's take advantage
of this opportunity.

132
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:32,994
It's a chance to clear up our image

133
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:40,710
and make sure our enemies
don't tarnish it again.

134
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:45,131
I'll go ahead, Governor.

135
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:46,841
All right. Be careful with that.

136
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:47,925
Yes, Governor.

137
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:52,180
[thudding]

138
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:02,190
[eerie music playing]

139
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:11,866
[screaming]

140
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:14,744
Who are you? Oh my God! Who are you?

141
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:16,329
[whimpering]

142
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:18,331
Ivy! Oh my God!

143
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:19,999
Hi, Emilia!

144
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,876
No! You cannot do this to me!

145
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:23,711
No! You're already dead!

146
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:25,671
But if I'm already dead, Emilia,

147
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:28,424
why am I still stuck in your head?

148
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,385
No! You can't hurt me, Ivy,
because you're dead!

149
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:32,929
You can't do this to me!

150
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:36,182
-That's what you think.
-No! No!

151
00:08:36,265 --> 00:08:38,226
-Bye, Emilia!
-No! No! No! No!

152
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:40,019
-I'm going to miss you.
-No!

153
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,688
-Don't die, Emilia!
-No!

154
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:46,526
-Don't leave me, Emilia.
-No! Ivy, no!

155
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:47,527
You can't do this!

156
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,986
No!

157
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:52,490
[gasping]

158
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:04,001
[exhales]

159
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:14,136
[car engine stops]

160
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,429
[car door opens]

161
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:23,229
[somber music playing]

162
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:27,066
[car door closes]

163
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:38,953
[somber music continues]

164
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,423
[Ivy] <i>Bastards!</i>

165
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,551
<i>All of you!</i>

166
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:55,303
[screaming]

167
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,929
<i>Bastards!</i>

168
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,019
From now on,

169
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,439
you are not getting inside my head.

170
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:11,777
Because dead people belong in the grave.

171
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:14,405
And, you are dead.

172
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:17,700
Dead. Dead. Dead!

173
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:21,370
[sighs]

174
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:31,172
[somber music continues]

175
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:52,693
[alarm clock ringing]

176
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,656
[ringing stops]

177
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:02,912
[instrumental theme music playing]

178
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:34,777
<i>Thank you, Lily.</i>

179
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,421
[Jepoy] Anna?

180
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:55,548
What's that?

181
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:03,556
Who's it from?

182
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:20,573
[music continues]

183
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:44,221
-Loring. Loring, come here.
-What?

184
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,140
Look at what's on our table. Quick!

185
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:48,309
What is it?

186
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,395
[Loring] Oh. What is it?

187
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,196
[woman] It's beautiful. Who's it from?

188
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:03,574
Emma! Emma!
Look at this! Come here, quick!

189
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:05,034
-What's happening here?
-Where is it from?

190
00:13:05,117 --> 00:13:06,535
The flower is so beautiful.

191
00:13:06,619 --> 00:13:08,078
-You have one too?
-Yeah.

192
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,872
-It's beautiful.
-Looks like everyone got one.

193
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:11,165
-Smells nice.
-You have one too?

194
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,917
-It smells nice.
-We all have one.

195
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,128
-Where are they from?
-Who do you think they're from?

196
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,671
Emma, who are these from?

197
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:19,089
-I don't know.
-How did they get here?

198
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:20,591
-Yeah.
-They got a flower too.

199
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:21,926
-They got a flower too.
-We all did.

200
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,260
-Where are these from?
-Yeah.

201
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:24,595
-Oh, it's beautiful.
-Smell it. It smells nice.

202
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,640
-It really smells nice.
-Who are these from?

203
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:29,683
-Look at it.
-It makes you wonder.

204
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:34,146
[music continues]

205
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,359
[no audible dialogue]

206
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:42,196
[music fades]

207
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:50,496
[suspenseful music playing]

208
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:53,332
J-Jenny!

209
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:56,252
Jenny! Jenny!

210
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:59,088
-Ma'am?
-Who's this from?

211
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:00,339
Who left that here?!

212
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:02,424
-Ma'am, I don't know.
-Who's this from?

213
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:06,387
Get that thing away from me!
Throw it away! Right now!

214
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:13,769
Emilia, your mansion's
feng shui is beautiful.

215
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:17,356
The positioning of the pool
and the seats are perfect.

216
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:18,399
Everything's perfect.

217
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,860
What about my political career?

218
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:23,863
I can see that your political star

219
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:26,156
and your career
will be wonderful this year.

220
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:30,160
I can see your father
handing you a good position.

221
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:31,954
-Really?
-Yes. Let's see.

222
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:35,082
-How about my love life?
-You have two love stars.

223
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,960
You will attract two men this year.

224
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,670
-Two?
-Two men.

225
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:42,381
Hmm… That's exciting, huh?

226
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:45,009
What more can you tell me, Master?

227
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:48,512
How about, um, this house?
Are the vibes good?

228
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,723
Yes. The feng shui
of this house is beautiful.

229
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,558
-[Julio] Is the car ready?
-Luck is good in this house.

230
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:54,018
Wait. Here is my Papa.

231
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,185
-Papa.
-Yes?

232
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:58,272
I'd like you to meet Master Hanz Cua.

233
00:14:58,355 --> 00:14:59,481
-Good afternoon.
-Governor Ardiente.

234
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,691
Good Afternoon, Master Hanz Cua.

235
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:03,068
-Good afternoon, Mr. Governor.
-I've heard about you. Yes.

236
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:06,155
-Yes, sir.
-Ah, I have to go.

237
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:07,615
Papa, where are you going?

238
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:09,658
We have technical rehearsals later.

239
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:12,244
I have some things to attend to.

240
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:15,497
I'll leave you here with the Master.

241
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:18,125
Sort out all the feng shui you want.

242
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:22,254
Um, excuse me.
Papa, can I ask you something?

243
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:26,175
Um, you know, now that Ivy Aguas is gone,

244
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:27,801
-Mm-hm.
-…are you still keeping your

245
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:28,802
promise?

246
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:33,682
Oh! Yeah, yeah, my promise. Don't worry.

247
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:38,312
I'm going to get back at that
Vice Governor Ruiz

248
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:40,230
for trying to oust me.

249
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:45,361
I will strip him of his position
and give it to you.

250
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:48,656
[exclaims] Thank you, Papa!

251
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:50,074
Oh, my gosh! Thank you, Papa.

252
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:53,327
And I am really, really sorry
for doubting you.

253
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,287
And I really apologize
for everything, Papa.

254
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:56,413
And thank you for giving me

255
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,123
this second shot in my life, Papa.

256
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,500
-Thank you so much, Papa.
-Yeah.

257
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:01,418
I have to go. I have to go.

258
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:04,713
[Julio grunts]

259
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,425
Master, did you hear what Papa said?

260
00:16:08,509 --> 00:16:10,219
-Yes, I did.
-You're so good.

261
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:13,514
He's going to give me back
my position as vice governor.

262
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:14,515
Yes.

263
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:16,016
So, when I become the vice governor

264
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,395
and then he becomes too old,
I'll be the governor.

265
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:20,270
-That's right.
-I knew it!

266
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:22,106
This is really my year.

267
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,774
-Yes.
-Let's go around some more.

268
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:25,818
-Okay. I'll check.
-Come. I'll give you a bonus.

269
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:29,071
Here. How about this painting?
Is it unlucky?

270
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:32,950
Do you know what you're
getting yourself into?

271
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:34,576
I do.

272
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:37,663
I wouldn't come here if I didn't.

273
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:41,834
I have strong evidence
against Julio Ardiente.

274
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:45,671
<i>Congressman, if you really want to win,</i>

275
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:47,131
<i>you have to make the investment.</i>

276
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:49,425
<i>I'm sure you'll earn back</i>
<i>whatever you invested</i>

277
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,093
<i>once you're governor, correct?</i>

278
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:52,720
<i>I'm only one call away, Congressman.</i>

279
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:54,763
<i>One call away from your victory.</i>

280
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,183
[chuckles]

281
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:02,396
Well, it looks like you have
everything figured out.

282
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:06,108
But the thing is, people who complain

283
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:08,068
about the election start out determined.

284
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:11,655
After a while, they lose their focus.

285
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:13,574
Their interest.

286
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:17,578
Others are even murdered
by the opposition…

287
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:19,997
to silence them.

288
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,331
[scoffs]

289
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,419
-Are you threatening me?
-Of course not.

290
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:28,130
I'm just telling the truth.

291
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:29,757
I'm not afraid.

292
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:32,509
I have the vice governor's support.

293
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:36,346
And I'm not the only one
against Julio Ardiente.

294
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:39,433
There's someone more powerful.

295
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:43,604
Someone more powerful
who's against your politics.

296
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:45,939
Who?

297
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:51,570
[tense music playing]

298
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:14,551
Commissioner, thank you
very much for your time.

299
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:23,644
[woman] Good morning, Governor.

300
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:24,728
Good morning.

301
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,856
[chuckles]

302
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:30,192
Of course.

303
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,027
Anytime.

304
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,963
-[man] Good morning, Governor.
-Good morning.

305
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,423
-Good morning, Governor.
-Good morning.

306
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:56,802
[tense music continues]

307
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:02,975
Commissioner?

308
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:07,104
[stammering] Governor,
I wasn't expecting you.

309
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,731
-Please, have a seat.
-Okay. Thank you.

310
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,154
[grunts]

311
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:19,908
Master Hanz, come on.

312
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:23,620
Feel free to roam around.
This is our dining.

313
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:27,666
Uh, Madam, should I dispose of these?

314
00:19:27,749 --> 00:19:29,418
Wait, let me check.

315
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,548
I miss you, Aunt Claire.

316
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,011
[pensive music playing]

317
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,476
Throw these out, and get out of my face.

318
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:53,442
[tense music playing]

319
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,322
[Emilia] <i>Please, don't!</i>

320
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:02,701
<i>Don't! Don't! Don't! Don't! Don't!</i>

321
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:07,080
<i>Who ordered you to kidnap me?</i>
<i>Who?! Answer me!</i>

322
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:08,999
<i>You won't stay here long, Mrs. Torillo.</i>

323
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,084
<i>We'll take you to Poblacion Ardiente</i>

324
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:12,711
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

325
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,260
[line ringing]

326
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,470
Romulo?

327
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:24,973
<i>Who is this?</i>
<i>Why do you have Claire's phone?</i>

328
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:28,852
It's me, Emilia.

329
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:30,854
<i>Listen carefully, Emilia.</i>

330
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:34,858
<i>Don't let Julio Ardiente get</i>
<i>a hold of Claire's belongings,</i>

331
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,610
<i>especially not her phone.</i>

332
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:40,280
Why? Aren't you one of Papa's men?

333
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,990
<i>I don't work for the Ardientes.</i>

334
00:20:43,116 --> 00:20:45,953
If you're not one
of Papa's men, who are you?

335
00:20:46,036 --> 00:20:48,956
Wasn't it Papa who helped me
get out of jail?

336
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,332
<i>Your father?</i>

337
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,709
<i>He's the one who had you imprisoned.</i>

338
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,503
<i>He didn't save you.</i>

339
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,547
<i>He wasn't the one who helped you.</i>

340
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:00,634
What?

341
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:04,805
[stutters] Papa didn't have
my case dismissed?

342
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:08,225
If not him, then who?

343
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,687
-Who?!
-[call dropped]

344
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:16,775
[line busy]

345
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:19,569
Oh, come on! What's with everyone today?!

346
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:23,991
[line ringing]

347
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:26,368
Hello? We need to talk.

348
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:33,333
As agreed upon,
here's your 50 million pesos.

349
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:37,254
And there's an additional 10 million…

350
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:41,675
for helping me win this election.

351
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:46,847
Governor, you know that I don't
always give out favors

352
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:50,100
to public officials who ask for my help.

353
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:52,978
I know that very well, Mr. Martel.

354
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:58,025
I know that you stick with
only the most powerful ones.

355
00:21:58,108 --> 00:22:01,236
Because power is more important
than money,

356
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:04,323
especially when that money runs out.

357
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:06,241
Very true.

358
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:10,412
Diego Torillo and Mateo Ruiz

359
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:12,372
aren't the only ones
you have to deal with.

360
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:16,877
Someone else has filed
a complaint against you.

361
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:18,045
[scoffs]

362
00:22:18,503 --> 00:22:20,380
Who?

363
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:25,677
Who else dared to go up against me?

364
00:22:27,179 --> 00:22:28,972
Lily Cruz.

365
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:32,476
[tense music playing]

366
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,695
[Anna] Jepoy?

367
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:45,155
Anna.

368
00:22:45,238 --> 00:22:48,075
Jepoy, what are you doing here?
Why didn't you join the others?

369
00:22:48,158 --> 00:22:49,409
I'm here to protect you.

370
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:54,122
I swore to myself and to Ivy that I would.

371
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:57,334
Anna, we have a problem.

372
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,587
You will be Julio's next target
when he finds out

373
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:02,923
the name of the person
who wants to overthrow him.

374
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,176
[Julio] <i>Lily Cruz?</i>

375
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:09,387
Lily Cruz is nothing.

376
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:11,556
Well, Governor, I have to tell you.

377
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:15,852
At this point, in my opinion,
Lily Cruz is a viable option.

378
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:20,315
Lily Cruz has got no power.
She's got no money.

379
00:23:21,399 --> 00:23:22,943
Governor, I hope you understand.

380
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:25,237
In my position,

381
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,531
I have to be open to the highest bidder.

382
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:30,450
I have to be willing to entertain

383
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:34,913
all those who come to me.

384
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:40,919
If it's money you need,
all you need to do is ask.

385
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:45,590
If I double the amount I'm giving you,

386
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:50,846
would that make you stop
entertaining those pesky insects

387
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:53,056
buzzing in your ear?

388
00:23:54,432 --> 00:23:55,767
How about it, Mr. Martel?

389
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:02,858
[phone ringing]

390
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:10,532
Jepoy, I can take care of myself.

391
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:14,911
You should go to whoever it is
that's calling you.

392
00:24:14,995 --> 00:24:17,372
Forget about that, Anna.
You're more important to me.

393
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:23,545
I'll never leave your side again.

394
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:27,257
[somber music playing]

395
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:43,857
Lily Cruz.

396
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:47,944
[tense music playing]

397
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,463
[Julio] <i>Hello, Colonel.</i>

398
00:25:06,546 --> 00:25:09,716
I want you to hunt down Lily Cruz

399
00:25:09,799 --> 00:25:12,510
<i>and make sure that woman</i>

400
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:15,222
can never cross me again.

401
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:19,935
I want her dead, as in yesterday!

402
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:21,144
Do you understand me?

403
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:22,854
Yes, Governor.

404
00:25:27,567 --> 00:25:30,153
[tense music playing]

405
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:33,907
Ivy Aguas is dead.

406
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:40,622
Lily Cruz is next.

407
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,501
-[tires screeching]
-[door opens]

408
00:25:48,546 --> 00:25:49,965
Let's split up!

409
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:52,342
You! Over there!

410
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:56,972
[Julio] <i>Once I've dealt with her,</i>

411
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:04,521
we'll go after everyone else
who keeps giving us problems.

412
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:08,525
No one can stop us.

413
00:26:09,776 --> 00:26:12,988
We will crush them like bugs!

414
00:26:15,657 --> 00:26:17,534
You will see, Arnaldo.

415
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:19,703
You will see.

416
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:32,716
Check there.

417
00:26:32,799 --> 00:26:33,883
On my signal.

418
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:44,060
[door opens, closes]

419
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:46,271
They aren't here.

420
00:26:46,354 --> 00:26:47,397
Let's go.

421
00:26:48,690 --> 00:26:49,774
There's no one out back.

422
00:26:50,775 --> 00:26:51,901
[line ringing]

423
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:53,570
Boss, they're not here.

424
00:26:55,405 --> 00:26:56,531
Keep looking.

425
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:01,828
It was the right decision
to leave the co-op.

426
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:05,123
Now, they're on the hunt for Lily Cruz.

427
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:07,959
This is getting too risky, Anna.

428
00:27:08,877 --> 00:27:11,463
Now, I'm sure Julio Ardiente
knows how "Lily Cruz"

429
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:12,922
is a threat to him.

430
00:27:14,966 --> 00:27:16,384
But this isn't news to us.

431
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:18,553
If your life was in danger before,

432
00:27:18,636 --> 00:27:19,846
it's worse now.

433
00:27:20,972 --> 00:27:22,140
We have to be extra careful.

434
00:27:22,223 --> 00:27:25,518
But I don't like all this
hiding and waiting, Jepoy.

435
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:26,853
What's the point

436
00:27:26,936 --> 00:27:29,189
if I'm just going
to hide here like a coward?

437
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:35,528
Anna, you're not alone.
We're in this together.

438
00:27:37,197 --> 00:27:40,158
You have to understand that this
is what we're supposed to do.

439
00:27:40,992 --> 00:27:42,452
Just have faith that we'll send each

440
00:27:42,535 --> 00:27:45,997
and every one of those Ardientes
to where they deserve.

441
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,291
That's a promise.

442
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:51,252
You know, I understand Miss Camia now.

443
00:27:51,336 --> 00:27:52,796
Now I know how she feels

444
00:27:52,879 --> 00:27:55,090
every time you tell her
to stay put and hide.

445
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:14,567
I heard the governor's
hunting Lily Cruz down.

446
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:18,696
If he finds her, I'm sure
he won't let her get out alive.

447
00:28:20,448 --> 00:28:22,992
Don't worry, Vice Governor. Lily's safe.

448
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:24,828
And it's all according to plan.

449
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:29,290
You can't tell me about your plans, right?

450
00:28:31,167 --> 00:28:35,964
Vice, I need you to trust in me.

451
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:40,343
Easy for you to say.

452
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:43,471
But how am I supposed to trust you

453
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:46,182
if you yourself don't trust me?

454
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:51,688
We reached out to you precisely
because you can be trusted.

455
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:54,899
And you're in the legal position
to determine the future

456
00:28:54,983 --> 00:28:57,277
of this province and its people.

457
00:28:57,944 --> 00:28:59,195
So, please, Vice.

458
00:28:59,821 --> 00:29:02,282
Please understand
that I can't tell you everything

459
00:29:02,365 --> 00:29:04,409
because there's too much at stake.

460
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:10,540
Let's just hope we don't fail.

461
00:29:10,623 --> 00:29:13,793
[tense music playing]

462
00:29:14,919 --> 00:29:19,883
This could be our last chance
to save this place.

463
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:32,353
Looking for something? What do you need?

464
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:34,022
We're out of food, Jepoy.

465
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:36,941
Don't worry. I'll take care of it.

466
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:38,943
But it's already lunchtime.

467
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:41,362
You heard me, right?

468
00:29:42,655 --> 00:29:43,948
I have to take care of something.

469
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:45,241
I'll buy food later.

470
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:47,660
There's a store right outside, Jepoy.

471
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:51,915
Yeah, I'll buy them later.

472
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:53,792
Just let me take care of this first.

473
00:29:56,377 --> 00:29:59,005
Don't go out, okay? It's dangerous.

474
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:04,886
[phone ringing]

475
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:05,887
Hold on.

476
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:34,666
[suspenseful music playing]

477
00:30:37,377 --> 00:30:38,503
Thank you.

478
00:30:40,463 --> 00:30:41,631
You know what, Jaguar?

479
00:30:42,048 --> 00:30:45,385
Until now, Papa's
still playing games with me.

480
00:30:45,468 --> 00:30:47,136
Well, I have a hunch…

481
00:30:48,429 --> 00:30:50,807
that Julio wasn't really
the one who saved you.

482
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:53,476
[scoffs] You know, what?

483
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,521
You're just saying that
because you hate him.

484
00:30:58,064 --> 00:31:00,024
You're too quick to forget, Emilia.

485
00:31:00,775 --> 00:31:03,027
Don't forget everything
Julio's done to you.

486
00:31:03,111 --> 00:31:05,071
How he disowned you.

487
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:09,367
Jaguar, I can still remember everything.

488
00:31:09,450 --> 00:31:11,744
I was there. I saw it all.

489
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:18,001
By the way, what's the news
on that Mercedes Palacio?

490
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:20,962
As of now, it's a dead end.

491
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:23,464
But, rumor has it…

492
00:31:24,507 --> 00:31:26,968
that it was Julio who
wanted to hunt down Lily Cruz.

493
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:28,428
[groans]

494
00:31:28,678 --> 00:31:31,598
What if she was the one who rescued you?

495
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:33,808
That's impossible, Jaguar.

496
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:38,146
Lily Cruz doesn't have the wits
or the resources to do that.

497
00:31:38,229 --> 00:31:42,775
I can even bet you my
multimillion jewelry collection

498
00:31:42,859 --> 00:31:44,444
that she couldn't have done it.

499
00:31:44,527 --> 00:31:45,695
No, it's not her.

500
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:48,573
It's impossible that she was
the one who helped me.

501
00:31:50,241 --> 00:31:52,201
Hmm… Tricky.

502
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:04,672
Miss, I'll have three cans of sardines

503
00:32:04,756 --> 00:32:06,132
and three packs of noodles.

504
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:07,425
Here you go.

505
00:32:07,508 --> 00:32:10,136
That's too much.
I don't have enough change.

506
00:32:10,219 --> 00:32:12,138
Sorry, but this is all I have.

507
00:32:17,352 --> 00:32:19,354
[man] Give me a pack of cigarettes, miss.

508
00:32:19,437 --> 00:32:21,356
[tense music playing]

509
00:32:28,988 --> 00:32:31,532
Miss, you forgot your change!

510
00:32:38,164 --> 00:32:40,583
Boss, I think I just saw Lily Cruz.

511
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,962
I'm here at District Sta. Ines.

512
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:46,839
Roger that. I'll follow her.

513
00:32:52,053 --> 00:32:54,764
[man] Hold it right there,
miss! Are you Lily Cruz?

514
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:57,141
[tense music playing]

515
00:33:07,610 --> 00:33:09,153
Lily Cruz.

516
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:13,366
Where do you think you're going?

517
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:18,079
There's no escape now.

518
00:33:30,174 --> 00:33:31,175
Grab her.

519
00:33:36,514 --> 00:33:38,683
-What's that way?
-An abandoned mansion.

520
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:40,018
Follow her.

521
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,020
[Jose] Get her.

522
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:43,938
[goon] Hurry.

523
00:33:48,192 --> 00:33:50,236
-[gunshots]
-[Anna yelping]

524
00:33:52,989 --> 00:33:54,115
Hey!

525
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:02,248
[goon] Hey! Stop!

526
00:34:19,974 --> 00:34:20,975
[exhales sharply]

527
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:22,727
You got some nerve.

528
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,522
You had to make me run.

529
00:34:29,859 --> 00:34:30,860
But, don't worry.

530
00:34:31,611 --> 00:34:35,740
Later on, we'll be running into you.

531
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:37,825
You're disgusting!

532
00:34:38,993 --> 00:34:41,204
I'd much rather die!

533
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:43,831
Die?

534
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:46,250
All right. What are you going to do now?

535
00:34:47,376 --> 00:34:48,753
Jump off this cliff?

536
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:51,589
Or get shot?

537
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,015
Well?!

538
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:05,019
[suspenseful music playing]

539
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,033
Follow her. Find her.

540
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:21,994
[tense music playing]

541
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:34,132
Boss, it's too steep. I don't
think she survived the jump.

542
00:35:34,215 --> 00:35:35,508
[Jose] Make sure.

543
00:35:35,883 --> 00:35:37,301
I think she's dead too.

544
00:35:37,969 --> 00:35:39,095
She's probably at the bottom.

545
00:35:40,471 --> 00:35:44,684
[gunshots]

546
00:35:51,274 --> 00:35:52,817
[phone ringing]

547
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:57,280
Hello, Governor?

548
00:35:58,030 --> 00:36:02,660
Colonel, is Lily Cruz still alive?

549
00:36:05,454 --> 00:36:06,956
She's dead, Governor.

550
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:08,416
Is that so?

551
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,793
You're sure she's dead?

552
00:36:16,048 --> 00:36:17,300
She fell off a cliff.

553
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:18,968
Yes, Governor.

554
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:23,097
Good job.

555
00:36:31,439 --> 00:36:35,318
[tense music playing]

556
00:36:56,964 --> 00:36:58,049
[whispers] <i>Anna.</i>

557
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:00,343
<i>Anna!</i>

558
00:37:00,801 --> 00:37:01,677
<i>Anna!</i>

559
00:37:03,304 --> 00:37:04,597
<i>Come on. Jump.</i>

560
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:21,948
Auntie?

561
00:37:27,453 --> 00:37:28,496
Diego.

562
00:37:29,580 --> 00:37:31,999
Did you hear the news
about Anna and Jepoy?

563
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:33,960
I did.

564
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:36,671
Thank God they're back at the safe house.

565
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:45,179
Uh, how was your meeting
with the vice governor?

566
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:51,018
He still doesn't believe we'll succeed.

567
00:37:52,561 --> 00:37:53,813
But I have high hopes

568
00:37:54,772 --> 00:37:56,607
that the vice governor won't let us down.

569
00:37:58,109 --> 00:38:01,988
How about the evidence
you gathered with Atty. Fisher?

570
00:38:02,071 --> 00:38:04,156
I'll go to Manila later

571
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:08,035
and bring the evidence
we collected to Secretary Martel.

572
00:38:10,204 --> 00:38:11,622
I have to go, Aunt Camia.

573
00:38:13,207 --> 00:38:14,625
Be careful, Diego.

574
00:38:16,127 --> 00:38:17,295
Don't worry, Aunt Camia.

575
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:22,091
I'll do whatever it takes
to finish Lily's fight.

576
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:25,970
We can do this.

577
00:38:29,932 --> 00:38:33,060
I never doubted that, Diego.

578
00:38:33,728 --> 00:38:34,687
Not once.

579
00:38:34,770 --> 00:38:38,941
[soft music playing]

580
00:39:08,804 --> 00:39:12,308
Lily Cruz is dead.

581
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:20,775
Another one bites the dust.

582
00:39:21,984 --> 00:39:22,985
[Julio chuckles]

583
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:28,282
[grunts]

584
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:42,505
Those bastards thought
they could get to me…

585
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:49,178
because of what they did to you,
and what they did to Emilia.

586
00:39:50,137 --> 00:39:51,138
Ha!

587
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:54,308
That's where they were wrong.

588
00:39:56,143 --> 00:40:04,026
They just made me more focused
and reignited the fire I had…

589
00:40:05,611 --> 00:40:06,946
when I was a young man.

590
00:40:07,905 --> 00:40:08,906
[Julio scoffs]

591
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:16,539
These stupid fools
just made me feel younger.

592
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:22,711
Now, you.

593
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:28,801
You.

594
00:40:32,763 --> 00:40:38,894
It's time for you
to wake up from your slumber.

595
00:40:41,188 --> 00:40:42,690
Don't forget…

596
00:40:44,817 --> 00:40:50,948
my blood runs through your veins.

597
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:55,453
The blood of a king.

598
00:40:57,371 --> 00:41:04,253
Blood that boils when someone
threatens to steal our throne.

599
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:09,508
Don't forget the people
who did this to you.

600
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:12,887
Use that hate…

601
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:21,604
so that you may rise, sit,
and rule by my side once again.

602
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:24,607
Use that hate.

603
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:28,944
Feel that hate.

604
00:41:30,946 --> 00:41:33,824
Keep that hate burning!

605
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:42,082
Come back to me, my dear young prince.

606
00:41:45,794 --> 00:41:48,047
I await your return.

607
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:56,347
[tense music playing]

608
00:41:58,807 --> 00:42:00,893
HAPPY CENTENNIAL,
POBLACION ARDIENTE!

609
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:03,312
[woman] <i>Don't forget to attend</i>
<i>the centennial celebration</i>

610
00:42:03,395 --> 00:42:06,106
<i>of our province with</i>
<i>Governor Julio Ardiente!</i>

611
00:42:08,275 --> 00:42:10,110
<i>There will be lots of food!</i>

612
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:12,655
<i>Don't forget to attend</i>
<i>the centennial celebration</i>

613
00:42:12,738 --> 00:42:15,407
<i>of our province with</i>
<i>Governor Julio Ardiente!</i>

614
00:42:19,578 --> 00:42:21,288
Make me gorgeous, Dylan, okay?

615
00:42:23,832 --> 00:42:26,293
[uplifting music playing]

616
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:27,586
I love it!

617
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:28,879
[Patricia] Madam!

618
00:42:28,963 --> 00:42:31,340
-Hey, Patricia.
-Here's your gown.

619
00:42:31,423 --> 00:42:33,926
It's beautiful! Just like you!

620
00:42:34,009 --> 00:42:35,135
[Emilia] Perfect.

621
00:42:35,469 --> 00:42:38,389
This is gonna be so fab and beautiful.

622
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:45,396
-So what's this about?
-This is from the governor.

623
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:49,900
[foreboding music playing]

624
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,991
[chuckles]

625
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:09,003
Please tell Governor Ardiente

626
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:10,963
that I'm looking forward
to his celebration.

627
00:43:11,422 --> 00:43:13,799
-Will do, Commissioner.
-Okay. Thank you.

628
00:43:15,884 --> 00:43:18,220
Jenny, where is my clutch bag?

629
00:43:18,762 --> 00:43:20,889
Faster! Faster!

630
00:43:21,390 --> 00:43:22,391
[groans]

631
00:43:26,770 --> 00:43:27,855
What?

632
00:43:29,982 --> 00:43:31,150
You look great.

633
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:33,527
Wow, Raul.

634
00:43:33,611 --> 00:43:37,072
Your flattery could use more work.

635
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:39,700
You know, your vocabulary is still so…

636
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:41,744
[Emilia yelps]

637
00:43:41,827 --> 00:43:46,749
[sensual music playing]

638
00:44:01,221 --> 00:44:02,765
Oh, please!

639
00:44:05,601 --> 00:44:07,478
Don't ruin this day.

640
00:44:13,025 --> 00:44:14,193
Opportunist.

641
00:44:15,527 --> 00:44:16,737
But you liked it.

642
00:44:20,658 --> 00:44:23,786
Jenny, my clutch bag! My god!

643
00:44:25,287 --> 00:44:26,372
Come on.

644
00:44:28,624 --> 00:44:31,001
And wipe that smile off your face.

645
00:44:36,131 --> 00:44:40,511
[marching band playing]

646
00:44:52,314 --> 00:44:54,608
[cheers, applause]

647
00:45:25,305 --> 00:45:26,306
[marching band stops]

648
00:45:30,561 --> 00:45:32,521
Good morning, everyone.

649
00:45:33,439 --> 00:45:37,776
Fellow citizens, my children, friends…

650
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:41,071
thank you for joining us…

651
00:45:42,364 --> 00:45:46,994
in paying tribute to my dear Esmeralda.

652
00:45:48,245 --> 00:45:49,413
You know…

653
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:54,793
before my beloved wife departed…

654
00:45:57,880 --> 00:46:02,843
she told me that she worried most…

655
00:46:05,262 --> 00:46:08,599
for her fellow citizens in this province.

656
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:14,938
Esmeralda truly loved you.

657
00:46:16,648 --> 00:46:19,818
So she entrusted your welfare to me.

658
00:46:21,528 --> 00:46:24,823
No matter what happens,
I will always take care of you.

659
00:46:24,907 --> 00:46:27,576
[applause]

660
00:46:32,915 --> 00:46:36,960
So, today, as we celebrate…

661
00:46:37,878 --> 00:46:42,925
our province's centennial,

662
00:46:43,759 --> 00:46:46,094
in front of Esmeralda's grave,

663
00:46:47,221 --> 00:46:48,972
I want her to know…

664
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:56,188
that I kept my promise
and fulfilled her will…

665
00:46:58,190 --> 00:47:02,861
to care for Ardiente's citizens.

666
00:47:03,946 --> 00:47:09,201
And I will continue to do so
for as long as I live.

667
00:47:09,284 --> 00:47:11,036
[applause]

668
00:47:11,119 --> 00:47:14,289
-We love you!
-Long live the Ardientes!

669
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:15,874
-We love you!
-We love you!

670
00:47:15,958 --> 00:47:20,003
-[pensive music playing]
-[man shouts indistinctly]

671
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:37,229
<i>Esmeralda was not your real mother.</i>

672
00:47:44,152 --> 00:47:46,655
<i>Who is my real mother, Papa?</i>

673
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:49,992
<i>And why are you keeping it from me?</i>

674
00:47:59,835 --> 00:48:00,669
Emilia.

675
00:48:02,963 --> 00:48:04,923
Hi, Mama. Are you there?

676
00:48:05,465 --> 00:48:06,508
Emilia.

677
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:09,303
Okay.

678
00:48:10,429 --> 00:48:12,764
You see, Mama, it's so sad.

679
00:48:13,682 --> 00:48:16,226
You're gone. You left us so early.

680
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:18,312
It's a shame.

681
00:48:18,687 --> 00:48:21,148
We could've had girl talks together.

682
00:48:21,481 --> 00:48:23,150
But, oh well.

683
00:48:23,650 --> 00:48:24,818
You were gone too soon.

684
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:28,947
I miss you, Mama.

685
00:48:41,918 --> 00:48:44,254
Citizens of Ardiente!

686
00:48:45,172 --> 00:48:50,260
We shall continue our celebration

687
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:55,641
of our province's one-hundredth year!

688
00:48:55,724 --> 00:48:56,892
[applause]

689
00:48:56,975 --> 00:49:00,604
[marching band playing]

690
00:49:00,687 --> 00:49:04,608
-[man] Governor, we love you!
-[supporters shout indistinctly]

691
00:49:21,541 --> 00:49:24,795
[host] <i>Let's all give a warm</i>
<i>round of applause</i>

692
00:49:24,878 --> 00:49:28,048
<i>for the Ardiente family!</i>

693
00:49:28,131 --> 00:49:31,968
<i>-Viva Ardiente!</i>
<i>-Viva Ardiente!</i>

694
00:49:38,266 --> 00:49:39,393
<i>Black is out!</i>

695
00:49:39,768 --> 00:49:41,561
<i>Gold is in.</i>

696
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:46,191
<i>Ivy Aguas is dead.</i>

697
00:49:46,274 --> 00:49:49,403
<i>But Lily Cruz is very much alive!</i>

698
00:49:49,486 --> 00:49:50,987
[indistinct chatter]

699
00:49:51,071 --> 00:49:53,323
<i>I am indestructible.</i>

700
00:49:53,407 --> 00:49:55,325
[theme music playing]
